{"availability":"available","full":"AngleSharp/AngleSharp","name":"AngleSharp","description":":angel: The ultimate angle brackets parser library parsing HTML5, MathML, SVG and CSS to construct a DOM based on the official W3C specifications.","category":"Design","language":"C#","stars":5542,"forks":598,"created":"2013-06-05T12:05:34Z","updated":"2026-10-15T14:05:21Z","license":"MIT","branch":"devel","homepage":"https://anglesharp.github.io","topics":["angle-bracket","anglesharp","c-sharp","dom","hacktoberfest","html","library","linq","parser"],"demo":"https://anglesharp.github.io/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T09:31:37.443Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T09:31:37.443Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T09:31:37.443Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T23:11:17.373Z","stars":5539,"forks":598},{"at":"2026-10-15T11:19:48.052Z","stars":5543,"forks":597},{"at":"2026-10-19T09:31:37.443Z","stars":5542,"forks":598}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["AngleSharp is a .NET library that gives you the ability to parse angle bracket based hyper-texts like HTML, SVG, and MathML. XML without validation is also supported by the library. An important aspect of AngleSharp is that CSS can also be parsed. The included parser is built upon the official W3C specification. This produces a perfectly portable HTML5 DOM representation of the given source code and ensures compatibility with results in evergreen browsers. Also standard DOM features such as querySelector or querySelectorAll work for tree traversal."],"features":["Portable (using .NET Standard 2.0)","Standards conform (works exactly as evergreen browsers)","Great performance (outperforms similar parsers in most scenarios)","Extensible (extend with your own services)","Useful abstractions (type helpers, jQuery like construction)"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AngleSharp/AngleSharp/blob/devel/README.md","fingerprint":"824ed5b33d692a701c59c624943af14d19c374e727ec4f56efecb